 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "복수 명사와 these / those",
   "en": "Plural nouns and these / those"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "대부분의 명사는 -s를 붙여 복수를 만듭니다: book → books. -s, -x, -ch, -sh로 끝나면 -es: bus → buses, box → boxes. man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet처럼 불규칙한 복수도 있어요. 가까운 것은 this / these, 먼 것은 that / those를 씁니다.",
   "en": "Most nouns add -s: book → books. Nouns ending in -s, -x, -ch, -sh add -es: bus → buses, box → boxes. Some plurals are irregular: man → men, woman → women, child → children, foot → feet. Use this / these for near things and that / those for far things."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "-s",
     "book → books"
    ],
    [
     "-es",
     "bus → buses, box → boxes"
    ],
    [
     "불규칙",
     "man → men, child → children"
    ],
    [
     "this/these, that/those",
     "These are my books."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "one thing: this / that, 여러 개: these / those.",
    "en": "One thing: this / that; many: these / those."
   },
   {
    "ko": "people은 이미 복수입니다: People are here.",
    "en": "People is already plural: People are here."
   },
   {
    "ko": "복수 명사에는 a / an을 쓰지 않습니다.",
    "en": "Don't use a / an with plural nouns."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "These are my books.",
    "ko": "이것들은 제 책이에요."
   },
   {
